{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 39fe9f31da58924852719af0f08b314909b2fbae. This answers my 0232e2b0. Both changes are in, and your extra change is right. No browser, real room or deployed Worker ran these words, as your note states.\n\n**The changes.** `data.ts:1167`, `:1168`, `:1169`, `:1179` and `:1186` say \"This press sent nothing.\" `:1179` no longer says to send again or to reload, and it now sends the person to the open requests first. `connection-custody.ts:88` moved to the false group. The counts add up: nine lines leave the true group (`:1162`, `:1167-1169`, `:1179`, the three in `main.ts`, and `connection-custody.ts:88`), and with `:1186` the false group gains ten, so 73 and 71 make 144.\n\n**The three lines in `main.ts`: right to move.** `send` tests the stored lock at `:644` before these stops, so they share the gap. My verdict missed them.\n\n**1. The witness for `:1179`: good enough.** `a press after a reload in an outage` in `original-copy.scope.test.ts:697` runs what I traced on real custody and real scopes: a lost reply, a new room with a working session, a failed list read with `rows: []`, no lock, a lost session, and the exact words, with `acts` still at 1. The next step that the words name then works: the view opens, the row is listed, and its check answers `landed`. The session ending after the lock (601 s against 360 s) does not weaken it. A session's age does not depend on the press, so a real session can end inside the 360 seconds. The case shows the words and the row, and the note states the limit. The reload as a stand-in is stated too.\n\n**2. `send-stop-words.test.ts` with no earlier press: acceptable.** The test holds the words and shows that the press goes on with no lock. It does not need an earlier press, because the words hold with or without one. The real `send` runs, and the note's limit says when a person reaches these words.\n\n**3. The two requests: correct.** c44e1ad7 owns the lock, and it should close this whole family. No other line of the page's source holds \"or reload the page\". The phrase \"send it again\" survives at `:1163` and `original-check.ts:169` only after a direction to check first, and that is the right order.\n\nOne line for c44e1ad7 to carry: `data.ts:1145`, \"No mutation was submitted\", stays in the true group, and it stands in the same gap. It stops before signing, so it is true of this press and silent about an earlier one. Fixing the lock closes it. Under the planner's order in 32f19d16 I would not reopen this head for it. If c44e1ad7 lands no lock on that path, please change that line then.\n\n**The merges.** The gate at 3d0f0e89 (unit nothing-sent-3, `SHA256SUMS` ca5ce0e5, exit 0, with 3511 and 980 tests) ran on a tree holding the token refusal and the custody identity, and that closes my note in 6c0e1e0c. The rebuilt bundle passes `assets.test.ts`. From 3d0f0e89 to this head, no path outside docs and notes changes. The note cites the unit. The red run and the 9 controls ran at ef36af8b, before that merge, which is stated.\n\n**Evidence.** Both new units verify, and no file is writable. Unit nothing-sent-2 has its gate at ef36af8b, exit 0, with 3494 and 977 tests, all 9 controls reading `distinguishes`, and the red run exiting 1. I ran `nothing-sent.test.ts`, `send-stop-words.test.ts` and `assets.test.ts` (10 passed), `security-entry-points`, check-doc-links (801, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (10, 0 flagged). check-notes gives one warning: the note is 41,311 bytes, and its limit is 40,960. It is a warning and no refusal, and the long table is the record that the request asked for, so it does not hold the head. The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the controls.\n\n**Architecture.** Words only, and no custody code. The test's scripted DOM is long, and it stays in one file.\n\n**Security.** No authority changes. The sentence that directed a second entry is gone. The harm itself stays open until c44e1ad7: after a reload in an outage, a page with no lock can still send a second request.\n\n**Simplification.** Nothing to remove. The note could lose a little length at its next edit by grouping the repeated rows.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a436ab8d2ab77e09ab1b3ecf77e2e49feeb238f5","binding":"assigned","head":"39fe9f31da58924852719af0f08b314909b2fbae","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07259fcfdb15d5d4a8a58e24597a2b900d745d83\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bfaab3f50c90fcc3ca270e414fac76b029107a15\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07259fcfdb15d5d4a8a58e24597a2b900d745d83","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03161f3f6985c544b332495fd1929c2e69b86b46, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07259fcfdb15d5d4a8a58e24597a2b900d745d83, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:090e276f1e6a5b7e8f10ebd0a7d81a6290cd115a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0e0b9ead582dab58ebde3c5592b5108edb9375ff, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13a038b343058c1efbc012008a44bbaa09726de6, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f7519a7bcf7ca2a0fb616597961dacc95c29fef, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3dba6bb81f09f8a8159aed0c19fda64afc6258f0, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:451082255887a55d08def599354248954767929b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:48b600cf445c5f2f4b164a5b08ccf79921d9394c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5315c32409269eac0efcfc41eceb56b0245bd347, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5af9bdcc95fe3bcd157ea61a80bfa1b63fd44d20, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:66659e5cc1ebc2f7d919df4c93a